1
00:00:00,548 --> 00:00:08,863
GlattTrack. Kashrut tracking in the slaughterhouse, from slaughter to the stamp. Every animal gets one number, and every station sees it.

2
00:00:09,922 --> 00:00:12,922
Chapter one: first installation

3
00:00:13,885 --> 00:00:18,947
An empty screen. We open the GlattTrack app on the team leader's tablet.

4
00:00:20,864 --> 00:00:27,111
The app connects to the plant server. The server has no team leader yet, so this is the first installation.

5
00:00:28,931 --> 00:00:34,690
Fill in the team leader's name, a personal code, and the server setup code from the installer.

6
00:00:40,765 --> 00:00:45,294
The server checks the setup code and approves the installation.

7
00:00:51,198 --> 00:00:57,902
This tablet is now registered as the team leader's device. The setup page opens, only this once.

8
00:00:59,822 --> 00:01:04,108
A recovery code. It can be skipped and made later.

9
00:01:06,296 --> 00:01:14,924
Choose the screens the plant uses: slaughter, esophagus, legs and head, inner, outer, small parts, and stamps. Then save.

10
00:01:28,312 --> 00:01:33,563
Workers, pairing the tablets, the owner and the printers can be done now or later.

11
00:01:36,777 --> 00:01:44,120
The team leader screen is open. A new plant starts with no kashrut statuses: every plant fills in its own.

12
00:01:46,250 --> 00:01:49,817
Chapter two: the plant's kashrut statuses

13
00:01:52,900 --> 00:02:01,044
In the settings: kashrut statuses. Every plant has its own kashrut: Glatt, Beit Yosef, MK, kosher, or any other name.

14
00:02:03,252 --> 00:02:07,788
Add a status: a name, and a group. Chalak, or not chalak.

15
00:02:10,982 --> 00:02:17,323
A name for the stickers, in Hebrew and in English, is optional. And a colour, from a large palette.

16
00:02:24,348 --> 00:02:31,267
Next to every status: chalak or not chalak, and its kashrut mark. What is deleted is gone for good.

17
00:02:33,449 --> 00:02:38,304
Tapping the name opens a rename, right there. No deleting and adding again.

18
00:02:41,268 --> 00:02:49,453
A plant that takes not chalak turns it on. A plant that does not, turns it off, and an animal that is not chalak is ruled treif.

19
00:02:50,641 --> 00:02:53,641
Chapter three: slaughter

20
00:02:57,322 --> 00:03:03,908
The slaughter tablet. The shochet presses one button per animal, and the next number fills in by itself.

21
00:03:12,614 --> 00:03:17,201
A question about the knife on animal five. Tap the question button.

22
00:03:20,556 --> 00:03:28,056
Number five is marked with a question mark and keeps blinking, so it is not forgotten. The shochet goes on to the next animal.

23
00:03:28,056 --> 00:03:31,056
Animal six: nevela.

24
00:03:34,612 --> 00:03:40,677
Animal eight: not chalak. At the outer ruling it gets only a not chalak status, or treif.

25
00:03:43,820 --> 00:03:47,526
The answer came. Tap five and rule it: slaughtered.

26
00:03:53,073 --> 00:03:59,807
Tapping a marked number opens a change, after a warning. Only until the number reaches the esophagus check.

27
00:04:12,758 --> 00:04:15,758
Chapter four: the esophagus check

28
00:04:19,200 --> 00:04:22,200
The esophagus check tablet.

29
00:04:24,068 --> 00:04:28,178
Trying to skip to animal three. The system does not allow it.

30
00:04:31,395 --> 00:04:34,775
Tap the blinking animal and choose OK.

31
00:05:06,139 --> 00:05:09,184
Chapter five: legs and head

32
00:05:13,076 --> 00:05:22,106
The legs and head tablet. Stickers are printed right after slaughter, before the ruling. It can also be split: one tablet for legs, one for the head.

33
00:05:22,106 --> 00:05:25,257
The first tap prints the leg stickers.

34
00:05:27,921 --> 00:05:35,196
The legs sticker. Printed: the number, the Hebrew and Gregorian dates, and the time. In the QR code: everything.

35
00:05:35,196 --> 00:05:38,366
The second tap prints the head sticker.

36
00:05:40,983 --> 00:05:44,247
The head sticker has the same details.

37
00:05:45,799 --> 00:05:50,230
Every animal in order. A nevela also gets a number sticker.

38
00:06:26,656 --> 00:06:29,656
The nevela sticker.

39
00:06:43,619 --> 00:06:46,756
Chapter six: the inner inspector

40
00:06:50,610 --> 00:06:54,884
The inner inspector's tablet. Tap the next animal in line.

41
00:06:56,779 --> 00:06:59,779
Rumen check: kosher.

42
00:07:00,957 --> 00:07:03,957
Maw: kosher.

43
00:07:05,098 --> 00:07:08,103
The lung drawing: mark it with a finger.

44
00:07:12,921 --> 00:07:17,625
Approve for the outer inspector. The animal moves on with its drawing.

45
00:07:30,053 --> 00:07:35,094
Animal three is treif. The first tap asks, the second tap rules.

46
00:07:43,935 --> 00:07:53,751
Animal four: a question on the maw. Tap the question button in that window. The number closes at once with a question mark. The check does not go on to the lungs.

47
00:08:00,638 --> 00:08:06,669
Animal four keeps blinking, marked: question, maw. The inspector goes on to the next animals.

48
00:08:06,669 --> 00:08:10,502
Animals five and seven: kosher, and approve.

49
00:08:40,078 --> 00:08:46,136
The answer came. Tap four: the maw window opens, and the check goes on from there to the lungs.

50
00:09:05,339 --> 00:09:08,339
Chapter seven: the outer inspector

51
00:09:12,115 --> 00:09:17,621
The outer inspector's tablet. The lung drawing is shown, and the inspector rules.

52
00:09:20,987 --> 00:09:23,987
Animal one: MK.

53
00:09:25,623 --> 00:09:31,048
Animal two: Beit Yosef. Four: Glatt. Five: kosher. Seven: Glatt.

54
00:09:52,021 --> 00:09:57,480
Animal eight, not chalak: only the plant's not chalak statuses appear, and treif.

55
00:09:59,939 --> 00:10:02,329
Ruled: Magen David.

56
00:10:02,329 --> 00:10:06,519
The ruling is made. Back to the legs tablet, for sorting.

57
00:10:11,501 --> 00:10:14,501
Chapter eight: leg sorting

58
00:10:20,574 --> 00:10:25,084
Leg sorting: scan the sticker that was printed before the ruling.

59
00:10:27,032 --> 00:10:31,679
The number is updated: the screen shows the current ruling from the server.

60
00:10:37,797 --> 00:10:40,937
Leg three: treif, in red.

61
00:10:45,704 --> 00:10:49,672
Chapter nine: small parts, and a USDA hold

62
00:10:53,569 --> 00:10:56,910
The small parts tablet: cheeks and tongue.

63
00:10:56,910 --> 00:11:01,021
Animal three is treif. The screen refuses to print.

64
00:11:04,266 --> 00:11:10,957
USDA hold: the tongue of animal one fell. Choose the tongue, then tap mark. No reason is needed.

65
00:11:18,735 --> 00:11:23,567
Animal one: both cheeks print. The tongue is held, so it does not print.

66
00:11:27,165 --> 00:11:32,329
The parts sticker: the ruling in Hebrew and English, and the MK kashrut mark.

67
00:11:32,329 --> 00:11:36,897
USDA released it. Tap release, and the tongue sticker prints now.

68
00:11:43,279 --> 00:11:46,279
Animal two: Beit Yosef.

69
00:11:49,137 --> 00:11:52,831
Beit Yosef, with its four kashrut marks.

70
00:12:03,504 --> 00:12:06,747
Chapter ten: stamps and weighing

71
00:12:10,551 --> 00:12:14,162
The stamps and weighing tablet, for the main carcass.

72
00:12:14,162 --> 00:12:18,389
Scan the animal's sticker. Five stamps print, by the ruling.

73
00:12:23,431 --> 00:12:27,677
The stamp of animal one: MK, with its kashrut mark.

74
00:12:28,260 --> 00:12:32,752
Weighing: scan the weight label, right side and then left side.

75
00:12:38,663 --> 00:12:42,519
Animal one is stamped and weighed. On to the next.

76
00:12:48,062 --> 00:12:51,062
Chapter eleven: the team leader

77
00:12:53,960 --> 00:12:58,392
Back with the team leader: the card of animal one, with its whole history.

78
00:12:59,801 --> 00:13:03,678
Every action: who, when, and from which tablet.

79
00:13:09,300 --> 00:13:17,209
The summaries: every kashrut status, treif by kind, maw, rumen and lungs, and nevela and shot, each on its own.

80
00:13:17,723 --> 00:13:20,451
Sample stickers, every kind.

81
00:13:20,451 --> 00:13:29,852
Top row: legs and head, before the ruling. Bottom row: parts and stamps, with the name in Hebrew and English on one line, and the plant's kashrut marks.

82
00:13:31,236 --> 00:13:34,236
Chapter twelve: behind the scenes

83
00:13:35,326 --> 00:13:43,894
Software updates: a tablet nobody is using updates by itself. A tablet in use asks, and updates after ten idle minutes.

84
00:13:44,955 --> 00:13:52,354
Without the plant server, work stops. What was tapped before the break is sent by itself when the connection returns.

85
00:13:53,441 --> 00:14:00,190
A backup every night, checked by a full restore. And the maker sees every plant on one screen, with alerts.

86
00:14:01,241 --> 00:14:06,095
GlattTrack. Every animal, every kashrut mark, in one place.
